    {
      "question": "e-4347",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "117200e0c824b7aa5263d408c3ab204bd5e640236249312e9ef114e440b51374",
      "new_sha256": "2bca013fe85523dac0c4fb24742817cf4a9c37fcb2ebb3b756bd872665325ec8",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-4347",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "First, we find the cross product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\times c & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 3-5\\cdot 2)i-(-1\\cdot 3-5\\cdot 1)j+(-1\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =-10i+8j-2k \\\\  & =\u27e8-10,8,-2\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the scalar triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\u27e82,-3,2\u27e9\\cdot \u27e8-10,8,-2\u27e9 \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-10)+(-3)\\cdot 8+2\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-48\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/example-4347.json",
          "file_sha256": "d4705456f237f065369fffd00b9c0e532f7ab38c6c7219209b6eb1c0b6db3770"
        }
      ],
