    {
      "question": "e-4348",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "eaeec63d0a57c7669c517238f6628fba65934fa8eae5989ff3b10e0993bb327f",
      "new_sha256": "da11cc39644e94430efea13985b4a1b280f8c33dc1b6ce30ab45b7ae1a58c39c",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-4348",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Remember that the scalar triple product $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c})$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $\\mathbf{a},$ $\\mathbf{b},$ and $\\mathbf{c}.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot (2\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-1))-2\\cdot (0\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-1))+(-1)\\cdot (0\\cdot (-1)-2\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =20-2-2 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039895/example-4348.json",
          "file_sha256": "922b032e0f89f05a5503894e6de4b750b9c2bb1ae6d144bfcb1284c21d61e247"
        }
